    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d124">

                <pb facs="0215" n="135" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg135"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A3/1798: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-07-15T19:00:00+01:00">July 15, 1936—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 15—2:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>348. An official note<anchor n="7" xml:id="d124-f1"/> was handed to me this
                    afternoon at the Foreign Office in which the British Government in the United
                    Kingdom invoked article 21 of the London Naval Treaty of 1930 with a view to the
                    retention of an additional 40,000 tons of overage destroyer tonnage over and
                    above that specified in article 16, clause 1, as not to be exceeded on the 31st
                    December, 1936. In conclusion the communication takes note of the statement in
                    the American memorandum of June 11<anchor n="8" xml:id="d124-f2"/> that in the
                    event of the British Government invoking article 21 the United States Government
                    would reserve the right deriving from this article to retain a proportionate
                    amount of excess tonnage in the destroyer class. Copy by pouch tomorrow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bingham</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d124-f1" n="7" xml:id="d124-f1-content">
                <p>Copy transmitted to the Department by the Ambassador in his despatch No. 2360,
                    July 16; not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d124-f2" n="8" xml:id="d124-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; see telegram No. 191, <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
